<title>POLAND: Polish construction rises 10.8 pct in June.</title>
<headline>Polish construction rises 10.8 pct in June.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction sales rose 10.8 percent in June after a 6.8 percent rise in May and was 20.2 percent higher than in June 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Construction sales rose 25.2 percent in the first half of the year against the first half on 1996.</p>
<p> POLISH CONSTRUCTION		JUNE	 MAY     JUNE 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	 10.8	 6.8	 11.3</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		 20.2	20.8	  9.8</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)    53.7	38.9	 36.4</p>
<p>NOTES: June 1997 had 22 working days, May had 21 working days and June 1996 had 20 days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
